1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
We will demonstrate to you how the pressure affects your outfit.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The pressure value will generate a constant force based on the front or back of the board.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
In this case, we create an inner line for the T-shirt, and then select the inner of the cologne layer to create the effect of the down jacket.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The surface of the inner layer is turned over and becomes the front or back of the cologne layer.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
When the pressure is set to the positive value, the board will receive a constant force from the front or back of the cologne layer.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Since the inner board is the opposite, it is now set to the same value to achieve pressure balance.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Note that when I change the pressure value, the pressure effect will become more subtle.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
In addition, if the inner layer of the board is not turned over, we will set the pressure value of the inner layer of the board to negative to balance the pressure.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Please make sure that the values ​​of the two layers of the inner and outer pressure values ​​are the same to balance the pressure.

